ter driving (Smugglers'' Notch VT-108 closed Nov-Apr); Epic/lift prices dynamic; Vail sites erroring at build time (verify)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Copley Hospital, 528 Washington Highway, Morrisville (~10 mi) - community hospital, 24/7 emergency services; higher-level trauma to UVM Medical Center, Burlington (~45 min)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"NO AVALANCHE CENTER governs Stowe (low-avalanche, patrolled, lift-served Eastern terrain - do NOT cite CAIC/UAC/BTAC/GNFAC; the Mt Washington Avalanche Center covers a DIFFERENT mountain in New Hampshire, not Stowe); ALTITUDE is LOW (Mansfield 4,395 ft - AMS not a factor); the winter spine is ICE/HARDPACK (''Eastern ice'' - sharp edges, ski in control, pronounced on the Front Four), extreme COLD + WIND CHILL on exposed Mount Mansfield (frostbite/hypothermia - layer, cover skin, warm-up breaks), and VERMONT WINTER DRIVING (VT-108 Mountain Road steep/winding; Smugglers'' Notch VT-108 closed Nov-Apr; winter tires/chains, check VTrans 511vt.com); self-guided Mansfield backcountry (Bruce/Teardrop) unpatrolled; tree-wells in glades","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'' Week, mid-winter weekends) + a big fall-foliage peak (late Sep-mid Oct)","shoulder":"early Dec (pre-holiday) + late-Mar/April spring skiing","green":"mud season (Apr-May) + Nov pre-snow; summer (golf, concerts, Rec Path) is a genuine third season, not a true low","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Lodge at Spruce Peak 3-6 mo (holidays + peak foliage longer); regular winter 2-4 mo; Epic by early fall