"stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"destination","entertainment":"destination","expedition":"destination","family":"destination","romance":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"primary"},"commission_lane":["consortia","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Stowe?","a":"**Vermont''s highest peak — Mount Mansfield (4,395 ft):** Stowe rides Mansfield plus adjacent **Spruce Peak**; the lift-served ski terrain tops out around **3,700 ft** (base ~1,559 ft; **~2,360 ft vertical**), with Mansfield''s true 4,395-ft summit rising above the lifts.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stowe_Mountain_Resort","accessed":"2026-07-19"},{"q":"How do I get to Stowe?","a":"**The legendary \"Front Four\":** Mansfield''s **Goat, Starr, National and Liftline** are steep, largely ungroomed runs with natural rock/tree hazards — collectively among the toughest lift-served trails in the Eastern US.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Mansfield","accessed":"2026-07-19"},{"q":"What is worth doing in Stowe?","a":"Cruise the Spruce Peak side — Spruce''s gentler, well-groomed terrain balances Mansfield''s steeps — the family/intermediate counterpoint on the same pass.","source":"https://www.sprucepeak.com/","accessed":"2026-07-19"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Stowe Ski Guide: Mount Mansfield, the Front Four & a Classic Vermont Village","meta_description":"Plan Stowe Mountain Resort, Vermont - the quintessential New England ski destination on the Epic Pass: Mount Mansfield (Vermont''s highest peak) and Spruce Peak linked by the Over Easy gondola, the legendary ''Front Four,'' the luxury Lodge at Spruce Peak, a picture-book village with the Trapp Family Lodge, and marquee fall foliage - with real timing, Eastern-ice/cold safety and booking intel.","slug":"stowe-vermont","primary_keyword":"Stowe Vermont ski travel gu