  ('winter-park-colorado', '12A', 'Winter Park', 'United States', 'Denver''s closest big mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Colorado Rockies', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Winter Park = City & County of Denver-owned, Alterra-operated / Ikon; Colorado''s longest continuously-operating resort (since 1939-40); Denver''s closest major (~67 mi via US-40/Berthoud Pass)","Seven territories incl. Mary Jane (legendary ungroomed moguls, opened 1975) + Parsenn Bowl + the extreme Vasquez Cirque; ~3,081 acres (1,212 off-piste), 171 trails, vertical 3,060 ft (base 9,000 / summit 12,060), 23 lifts + 10-person gondola","~344.6 in (~8.75 m) snowfall; steep split ~8 beg/18 int/19 adv/52 most-difficult/3 expert-only; longest run 4.9 mi (Parsenn Bowl); no night skiing","The Winter Park Express - Amtrak SKI TRAIN from Denver Union Station to a ski-in platform (57 round trips 2025-26; Thu-Sun + holidays via Moffat Tunnel)","NSCD (National Sports Center for the Disabled) based here since 1970 - one of the world''s largest adaptive-sport orgs, deep Paralympic-medal legacy","BACKCOUNTRY: NO powder cat-skiing at the resort - Vasquez Cirque is hike-to / Cirque-Sled transport (boundary aid, not guided cat-ski); off-resort cat via Jones Pass Guides; Berthoud Pass hike-to BC","Lodging is CONDO/mid-range, NOT 5-star flags - a value, less-crowded alternative to the Vail/Summit corridor; NO natural hot springs on-site (Hot Sulphur ~27-31 mi)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: heavy Front-Range volume by consensus, not published; CAIC ''Front Range'' zone; Middle Park Health Fraser campus (24/7 ER, opened Jun 2025)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Middle Park Health - Fraser campus (Winter Park/Fraser border, opened Jun 2025) - 24/7 ER, trauma bays, helipad; Granby (surgical) + Kre