10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to blackdiamondequipment.com (AvantLink); trail maps also sold at the park","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":56,"blurb":"NPS: \"Do not rely on your phone for maps or flashlights. Limited cell service, GPS, and flashlight use drain batteries quickly.\" \"Consult a topographic map before hiking. Do not rely on the park handout map.\""},{"name":"Water treatment for Duck Harbor on Isle au Haut","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","expedition"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":57,"blurb":"NPS: \"There is no potable water source at Duck Harbor Campground. Plan ahead to treat the water or bring enough potable water for the duration of your stay.\""},{"name":"Cadillac Mountain Sports","source":"https://www.cadillacsports.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","ocean"],"booking_route":"walk-in retail, Bar Harbor and Ellsworth","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":58,"blurb":"\"Maine''s Performance Outfitter\" with stores at 26 Cottage St., Bar Harbor, and in Ellsworth, plus Cadillac''s The North Face at 39 Cottage St.: \"our staff is here to help you select the best gear and apparel for outdoor adventures.\""}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you need reservations for Acadia National Park?","a":"Only for Cadillac Summit Road by vehicle. The NPS states: \"Vehicle reservations are required for Cadillac Summit Road from Wed May 20 through Sun Oct 25, 2026.\" They cost $6 and are \"sold online in advance at Recreation.gov. They are not available for purchase at the park.\" \"Vehicle reservations are not required for any other areas of the park, or for visitors who enter the area by foot, bike, or taxi.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/vehicle_reservations.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How much is an Acadia National Park pass?","a":"Per the NPS: private vehicle $35, motorcycle $30 and per person $20 (on foot or bicycle), each valid 7 days; the Acadia annual pass is $70. Non-US residents pay a \"$100 per person fee\" in addition to the entrance pass, and the Cadillac Summit Road reservation is $6.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you visit Acadia National Park without a car?","a":"Yes, by the Island Explorer: \"The fare-free Island Explorer features bus routes linking hotels, inns, and campgrounds with destinations in Acadia National Park and neighboring village centers.\" \"Spring service on the Gateway Center, Loop Road, and Schoodic routes begins May 20, 2026. Other Island Explorer buses operate from June 23 through October 12, 2026.\"","source":"https://exploreacadia.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Acadia National Park for fall foliage?","a":"The NPS says \"The peak generally comes in mid-October\" and points visitors to Maine''s fall foliage website, updated every Wednesday in season. Fall weather is \"Variable weather; 30-70 F (-1-21 C)\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/weather.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp in Acadia National Park?","a":"Yes, at Blackwoods, Seawall, Schoodic Woods and Duck Harbor. \"All campsite reservations must be made in advance at Recreation.gov\"; for the first three, \"90 percent of campsites are released six months in advance on the first of each month at 10 am\" and the rest 14 days ahead. \"There is no backcountry camping, ''out-of-bounds'' camping, overnight parking, or winter camping allowed anywhere in Acadia.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Acadia National Park dog friendly?","a":"The NPS states: \"There are 100 miles (161 km) of hiking trails and 45 miles (72 km) of carriage roads in the park where pets are permitted.\" Pets \"must be kept on a leash no longer than 6 feet (2 m) at all times\", and six trails, including the Precipice and Beehive, are closed to pets.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Acadia National Park open in winter?","a":"Parts of it. The NPS operating table closes the Park Loop Road and paved roads from Dec 1 to Apr 15 and unpaved roads from Nov 15 to May 15, while the Schoodic Loop and Point Road are listed \"Year-round\" and the carriage roads \"Year-round, seasonal closures\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/acad/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Acadia National Park: Cadillac, Carriage Roads & Bar Harbor | TravelWell","meta_description":"Cadillac Summit Road reservations, carriage roads, Schoodic and Isle au Haut, plus the Bar Harbor ring: campgrounds, RV parks, Under Canvas and brand hotels.","slug":"acadia-national-park-maine","primary_keyword":"Acadia National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Acadia National Park, Maine"}}'::jsonb, 34)
