e/127241/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","ocean","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - a public waterfront street","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"\"The Nautical Mile in Freeport is one of the hottest destinations for food and summer fun on Long Island\" - \"dozens of restaurants, bars, shops and recreational hot spots\" and charter fishing boats along Woodcleft Avenue"},{"name":"Captain Lou Fleet","source":"https://www.captloufleet.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","group","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"Peek (book.peek.com) from the own website","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"31 Woodcleft Avenue, Freeport: \"Daily Fishing Trips: Half-day, full-day, and night excursions targeting fluke, sea bass, striped bass, tuna, and more\", plus whale and seal watching cruises, sunset party cruises and private charters; boats include Captain Lou VII and Starstream VIII; (516) 623-5823"},{"name":"The Codfather Fishing Charters","source":"https://www.codfatherfishing.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","adventure"],"booking_route":"phone (516) 868-9073 or Facebook","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"guide","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"\"6 Passenger Saltwater Fishing Charters\" \"Based out of Freeport Long Island New York off of the Nautical Mile (Woodcleft Ave)\", running \"YEAR-ROUND\" from winter tog and herring to the fall striped bass run; Captain Mike Barnett; (516) 868-9073"},{"name":"Nautilus Cafe","source":"https://www.nautiluscafe.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"OpenTable or phone 516.379.2566","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"46 Woodcleft Avenue, Freeport: seafood on the Nautical Mile - pecan-crusted orange roughy, jumbo lump crab cakes, broiled marinated scallops, with duck and prime rib for landlubbers; lunch Tue-Sat noon-4, dinner nightly; 516.379.2566"},{"name":"The Clam Bar, Point Lookout","source":"https://www.pointlookoutclambar.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone (516) 670-9717","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"\"From Our Ships… To Your Lips!\" - a dockside seafood restaurant and market at Point Lookout with clams, sushi and family fare; open 7 days year-round, \"We Never Close\"; (516) 670-9717"},{"name":"Salt Shack","source":"https://www.saltshackny.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","entertainment","ocean"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone (631) 422-7222","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"100 Ocean Parkway, Babylon: \"Live Music, Food & Drinks on Cedar Beach, NY\"; open May through September, Fri 4-11 PM, Sat 11 AM-11 PM, Sun 11 AM-9 PM, \"closed Monday-Thursday for the remainder of the 2026 season\"; (631) 422-7222"},{"name":"Atlantica at the Allegria Hotel","source":"https://longislandpress.com/2022/07/14/19-oceanfront-long-island-restaurants-to-get-your-vitamin-sea","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"via the hotel, 516-889-1300","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"80 West Broadway, Long Beach: \"The signature restaurant of the Allegria Hotel, Atlantica''s chic design and gourmet New American menu have made it a favorite among locals\", open year-round (Long Island Press, 2022). The hotel''s own page names an \"upscale restaurant and lounge\" but not the name Atlantica."},{"name":"Long Beach boardwalk and Ocean Beach Park","source":"https://www.longbeachny.gov/beach","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","family","culinary"],"booking_route":"city beach pass (rates not read)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"the \"City by the Sea\" \"boasts a stunning white sand beach\" and a \"vibrant 2.1-mile boardwalk\" with dining, shopping and nightlife; lifeguards May 23-June 14 weekends only, then seven days a week June 19-September 7; designated surfing beaches"},{"name":"Beach umbrella and sun protection","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/jones-beach-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to amazon.com (Associates) or rei.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"NY State Parks for Jones Beach: \"Lounge Chair Rentals & Umbrella Rentals Available 5/23 - 9/20 $15 Rental\". The agency''s summer advice: \"Avoid contact with vegetation, wear sunscreen, and approach your outings with your own physical limitations in mind.\" (https://nystateparks.blog/2025/05/20/know-before-you-go-tips-for-safe-fun-outdoor-recreation-this-summer/) Bring your own umbrella outside the rental season."},{"name":"Life jacket for non-swimmers in open water","source":"https://nystateparks.blog/2025/03/19/ready-set-swim-safely/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink) or amazon.com (Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Jones Beach lifeguard Cary Epstein, on the NY State Parks blog: \"If your child isn''t a strong swimmer, they should wear a properly fitted U.S. Coast Guard-approved life jacket in open water settings. Floaties and inflatable toys are not substitutes for safety equipment!\" \"Make sure you ask your local lifeguard first if these are permitted.\""},{"name":"Fishing and crabbing kit for the Field 10 piers","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/details.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to DICK''S Sporting Goods (AvantLink); bait at the Field 10 shop","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":9.25,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"NY State Parks: \"Field #10, fishing piers and a fully equipped bait and tackle shop enable fishing and crabbing until sunset.\" \"The regional Night Fishing Permit is required after sunset.\""},{"name":"unsOund Surf, Long Beach","source":"https://www.unsoundsurf.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"surfboard rental booked online on the shop site; walk-in shop","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"\"New York''s #1 Surf Shop\", open \"since 1997\": \"HIGH QUALITY SURF PRODUCTS / SURFBOARD AND WETSUIT RENTALS / LESSONS / REPAIRS\"; new and used surfboards, wetsuits, rashguards and sunglasses, with surfboard rentals booked online. Telephone 516-889-1112. Jones Beach allows surfing \"at several locations along the beachfront\"."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Jones Beach State Park free?","a":"Not for a car: the park charges a vehicle use fee of \"$8 per car 4/4-5/22 & 9/14-11/8 / $10 per car 5/23-9/13\"; buses pay $35. An Empire Pass card is $80.","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/jones-beach-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Are dogs allowed at Jones Beach State Park?","a":"No. New York State Parks states: \"No Pets Allowed All Year Round.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/details.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Jones Beach State Park?","a":"Yes, in season: the ocean beaches open seasonally (5/22-9/20 on the park page), and \"Swimming is allowed only when lifeguards are on duty.\" Zach''s Bay \"provides a calmer swimming experience for small children.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/jones-beach-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Jones Beach State Park have a pool?","a":"Two: \"West Bathhouse Pool: 6/27-8/26\" and \"East Bathhouse Pool: 6/27-9/7\". Admission is \"$5 for adults\" and \"$3 for children and seniors.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/amenities.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What town is Jones Beach State Park in?","a":"Its address is \"2400 Ocean Parkway, Wantagh, NY 11793\", in New York State Parks'' Long Island Region, \"less than 20 miles from New York City.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/energy-nature-center.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How many acres is Jones Beach State Park?","a":"\"More than 2,400-acres of maritime environment on the south shore of Long Island\", with \"6.5 miles of beautiful white-sand beach on the Atlantic Ocean.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/jones-beach-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When did Jones Beach State Park open?","a":"New York State Parks says: \"Jones Beach State Park and Jones Island...were the creation of master builder Robert Moses in the 1920s.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/details.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What time does Jones Beach State Park open?","a":"Hours vary by facility and season. The Central Mall and Zach''s Bay playground are open \"Year round, sunrise-sunset\", and the Jones Beach Energy & Nature Center operates \"Daily 9am-4:30pm\".","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/parks/jonesbeach/energy-nature-center.aspx","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is the Jones Beach light show, and how do tickets work?","a":"The Magic of Lights drive-through 2025-26 edition \"opens Nov. 21 and runs nightly through Jan. 3\", Sunday-Thursday 5-10 p.m. and Friday-Saturday 5-11 p.m.; tickets were $30 in advance, $35 at the gate on weekdays and $40 on weekends (News 12, 19 November 2025).","source":"https://longisland.news12.com/2025/11/19/magic-of-lights-returns-to-jones-beach-with-its-brightest-display-yet/ALgNJPXoe9OElmNLs2mFb","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Jones Beach State Park: Beach, Pools, Theater & Nearby Stays | TravelWell","meta_description":"6.5 miles of Atlantic beach, two pools, Zach''s Bay, the Jones Beach Theater and July air show, plus campgrounds, charters and hotels nearby.","slug":"jones-beach-state-park-new-york","primary_keyword":"Jones Beach State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Jones Beach State Park boardwalk water tower"}}'::jsonb, 36),
  ('letchworth-new-york', '12A', 'Letchworth State Park', 'United States', 'Grand Canyon of the East and its waterfalls', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'New York State & the Hudson', '{"hiking","family","romance","adventure","culture","glamping","parks"}', '{"dramatic","pastoral","family-friendly","historic"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"Middle Falls, below the Glen Iris Inn","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior","romance"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"the 107-foot Middle Falls, \"the largest of the falls in the park, and the only one you can stand alongside to enjoy its beauty and power\", viewed from the Glen Iris Inn; the Portageville (South) entrance gives \"Access to the Glen Iris Inn, Museum, Middle and Upper Falls Area\" per the park"},{"name":"Gorge Trail (Trail 1)","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - public trail; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"This 7-mile long trail starts at the Genesee Arch Bridge near the Portageville entrance and runs along the gorge passing by the Upper, Middle, Lower and Wolf Creek Falls, as well as Inspiration Point, Archery, Big Bend and Tea Table overlooks\"; the park lists a permanent closure of \"Trail 7 from Middle Falls to the Genesee Arch Bridge\""},{"name":"Inspiration Point Overlook","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","family","romance","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - roadside overlook; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"look down into the Gorge and see the Middle Falls, Upper Falls and the Genesee Arch Bridge spanning the Genesee River\"; a stop on the 2026 free fall shuttle"},{"name":"Upper Falls and the Genesee Arch Bridge","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","rail"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"The southern-most waterfall, the Upper Falls is 70 feet tall and located below the Genesee Arch Bridge near the Portageville main entrance\"; the county FAQ: \"Access to the Genesee Arch railroad bridge is absolutely prohibited as it is private property\""},{"name":"Lower Falls and the Stone Arch Bridge","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/education-history-at-letchworth","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","culture","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - public trail; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"the 70-foot Lower Falls, reached \"by parking near the Lower Falls Restaurant and hiking south along the Trail 1 (Gorge Trail)\" and down stairs; the Stone Arch Bridge, \"Constructed in 1935 by the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC)\", \"serves as the only pedestrian crossing of the Genesee River in Letchworth State Park\""},{"name":"Wolf Creek Falls, Tea Table, Great Bend and Archery Field overlooks","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - roadside overlooks; $10 vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"Wolf Creek \"cascade[s] over the edge as it slithers 225 feet down into the gorge\"; Great Bend \"overlooks one of the deepest section of the gorge\"; Tea Table has \"tables, grills and a shelter\"; Archery Field is \"immediately south of the Castile entrance\""},{"name":"Finger Lakes Trail, Letchworth branch","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/explore-the-outdoors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - public trail; guided treks listed on the park events page","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"\"The longest continuous trail in Letchworth is the 24-mile long Finger Lakes Trail, running the entire east side of the park from Portageville to Mt. Morris\"; the park runs guided \"Finger Lakes Trail Treks\" as \"Moderate to difficult level outings\", the next on October 8, 2026 (Dishmill Section)"},{"name":"Glen Iris Inn and Caroline''s Dining Room","source":"https://www.glenirisinn.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","culinary","senior","culture","wine"],"booking_route":"own website booking; phone 585-493-2622; dining reservations through the inn''s website per parks.ny.gov","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":5,"fit_rules":{"duration":"overnight or a meal","before":"reservation; in October keep the confirmation ready at the gate","after":"walk to Middle Falls","pairs_with":"Middle Falls, Inspiration Point, the museum","pace":"leisurely","time_season":"May 1 to October 31, 2026 per parks.ny.gov"},"blurb":"\"Formerly the country estate of William Pryor Letchworth, the Glen Iris Inn has welcomed guests as a country inn since 1914\", overlooking Middle Falls; 15 guestrooms and suites; \"Caroline''s Dining Room at the Inn serves breakfast, lunch and dinner daily from May 1st through November 2nd\"; Fall Winemaker''s Dinner \"$99 per person inclusive of sales tax and service charge\""},{"name":"Glen Iris cottages and lodges (Pinewood Lodge, Pinewood Lofts, Caroline''s Cottage, Stone House, The Chalet)","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/camping-luxurious-accommodations-at-letchworth","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","romance","group","glamping"],"booking_route":"Glen Iris Inn website or phone (585) 493-2622","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"Pinewood Lodge''s \"7 luxury efficiencies\"; two Pinewood Lofts with gas fireplace and \"2-person whirlpool tub\"; Caroline''s Cottage (max six); the Stone House \"directly across from Inspiration Point\" (max eight); and the three-bedroom Chalet - all booked through the Glen Iris Inn"},{"name":"Letchworth park cabins (Areas A-E)","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking","group"],"booking_route":"Reserve America (newyorkstateparks.reserveamerica.com) or 1-800-456-2267","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"cabins \"Available from May 8, 2026 - November 29, 2026\"; \"$59.50-$156 per night, 2-night minimum outside peak season\", \"$238-$596 per week during peak season, only weekly rentals permitted\"; out-of-state fee $7 per night; pets allowed in Cabin Area C only"},{"name":"Highbanks Camping Area","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"Reserve America or 1-800-456-2267","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"all 270 Tent and Trailer Campsites\", entered by the Camping Entrance or the Perry (West) entrance; \"$30-$32 per night, 2-night minimum\" plus $5 per night out-of-state fee; campground May 15 to October 12, 2026; loops 300-600 and 800 closed for shower-building construction \"tentatively, until July 2, 2027\""},{"name":"Parker''s Hideaway","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group","culture"],"booking_route":"camping office 585-237-3303 or park office 585-493-3600; dates on Reserve America","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"\"The former Civilian Conservation Corps-built building located just North of the ''C'' Cabin Area\", two bedrooms and two baths, sleeps six, air conditioning, linens not provided; $1000 per 5-day week (Friday-Wednesday), or non-peak $300 per night with a 2-night minimum"},{"name":"Genesee Conference Center","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","wellness"],"booking_route":"park office reservationist, (585) 493-3600","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"\"Located in a secluded area at the southwest portion of Letchworth State Park\", with \"a spacious country lodge room, bedrooms, bathrooms with showers and a kitchen\"; open year-round for \"professional and organizational retreats\", reserved through the park office"},{"name":"Humphrey Nature Center","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","wildlife","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - walk-in; free programmes on the park events page","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"interactive exhibits that which highlight the plants and animals, geology and river ecology\"; outdoor classroom, butterfly garden and bird observation station; trails lead to Trout Pond and Inspiration Point Overlook; open daily 10:00 am-5:00 pm"},{"name":"Autism Nature Trail (The ANT)","source":"https://autismnaturetrail.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","wellness"],"booking_route":"none needed - open in park hours; check the ANT calendar","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"a one-mile looped main Trail with eight stations at various intervals, offering a range of experiences from quiet engagement to active exploration and adventure\"; beside the Humphrey Nature Center, via the Castile entrance (6787 County Rd 38); \"5th ANTiversary Event\" Friday, October 9th, 2026"},{"name":"William Pryor Letchworth Museum","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/education-history-at-letchworth","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","senior","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - walk-in, donation","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"The Stone Museum is located across the road from the Glen Iris Inn and contains artifacts and information about the park, the native people that inhabited the Genesee River Valley area, and the life of William Pryor Letchworth\"; May-October, 10:00 am-5:00 pm; donation $1 adult, $.50 child, $3 family per parks.ny.gov"},{"name":"Council Grounds: Seneca Council House and Mary Jemison''s cabin","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - public historic site in the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"the park: Mary Jemison (Dehgawanus) \"lived and farmed the flats here\" after the 1779 Sullivan-Clinton Campaign; William Pryor Letchworth \"had her remains brought to what is now Letchworth State Park, commissioned a statue to honor her\"; \"The park also contains a cabin Mary built for her daughter as well as the Seneca Council House\""},{"name":"G.W. Harvey Swimming Pool","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"none needed - included in the vehicle entrance fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"the park''s pool on the north end, reached by the Mt Morris (North) entrance; 2026 season \"Projected opening 6/27 - Labor Day\", 11:00 am-6:45 pm; \"Pool & Museum included!\" in the $10 vehicle fee; the county FAQ: \"Swimming in the Genesee River is prohibited\""},{"name":"Balloons Over Letchworth (Liberty Balloon Co.)","source":"https://www.libertyballoon.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","romance","senior"],"booking_route":"own website booking (''Book Online''); phone (585) 493-3340 or 585-243-3178","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"fit_rules":{"duration":"a dawn or dusk flight","before":"booking and the operator''s physical requirements","after":"Glen Iris Inn breakfast or dinner","pairs_with":"Middle and Upper Falls","pace":"leisurely","time_season":"May through mid-October, at dawn and dusk, weather permitting"},"blurb":"\"Offering spectacular balloon rides over the Park since 1987\", \"Operated by family-owned Liberty Balloon Co. since 2019\"; rides \"From $445/person\"; launches \"highly dependent on regional wind and weather conditions\", and watching a launch is free; the county calls it \"the official hot air balloon company of Letchworth State Park\", flying \"May through mid-October\""},{"name":"Adventure Calls Outfitters (Genesee River rafting)","source":"http://www.adventure-calls.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","river","family","group"],"booking_route":"phone 1 (888) 270-2410 or email aco.rafting@gmail.com; 50% deposit","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"the county: \"the only rafting company in the park\" and \"The Genesee River is the perfect paddle for novice rafters and great for family and teambuilding outings\"; its own site: rafting office inside the park, \"Helmets are mandatory for all of our river trips\", \"A 50% deposit is mandatory when making a reservation\", flip flops and slides not allowed"},{"name":"Mount Morris Dam tour and Overlook","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/education-history-at-letchworth","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"online ticket registration linked from the county page; phone (585) 658-4790","commission_status":"none","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"a ranger-guided walking tour of about an hour with \"a steep 1 mile trek into the Genesee River Gorge to the top of the Mount Morris Dam\", then \"an elevator down 200 feet into the dam\"; April-October, Monday-Thursday 2:00 p.m., Friday-Sunday 11:00 a.m. and 2:00 p.m.; tickets up to 7 days ahead; 6103 Visitor Center Rd, Mt Morris"},{"name":"Free Fall Leaf Shuttle, October 2026","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/blog/letchworth-state-park-fall-guide-traffic-parking-shuttle","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - free, no reservation","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["move"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"\"RTS will offer free shuttle service for park visitors on select October weekends\": October 3 & 4, 10 & 11, 17 & 18, 11:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m., stopping at Lower Falls, Trailside / Nature Center, Inspiration Point, Glen Iris Inn and Middle Falls / Upper Falls; \"subsidized by Letchworth State Park, Glen Iris Inn and Letchworth Concessions LLC\""},{"name":"Winter at Letchworth: snow tubing, cross-country skiing, snowmobiling","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed; a night-time snowmobile permit is posted among the park documents","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"the park: \"Winter activities include snow tubing, cross-country skiing, and snowmobiling\"; the county FAQ: \"There is a tubing hill located near Trailside Lodge. Patrons must bring their own inflatable tube\" and snowmobiling is \"on designated trails only\""},{"name":"Lower Falls Restaurant","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/blog/letchworth-state-park-fall-guide-traffic-parking-shuttle","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"the restaurant by the Lower Falls parking area, named by the county as a shuttle stop (\"Lower Falls / Lower Falls Restaurant\") and as the parking point for the Lower Falls walk"},{"name":"Adventure Bound Four Winds, Portageville","source":"https://abcamping.com/abfourwinds/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"own website booking (''Book Now'')","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"\"a family camping resort located at 7350 Tenefly Road in Portageville, New York, just minutes from Letchworth State Park\"; deluxe cabins that sleep six, premium RV rentals \"New for 2026\", full-hookup and tent sites; inflatable water slides, heated pool, on-site stream for fishing; \"Open seasonally from May through October\""},{"name":"The Ridge Campground, Mount Morris","source":"https://theridgecampground.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"own website ''Reserve Now''; phone 585.658.4709","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"\"a family-friendly camping facility nominated in the Top 5 Stay-Cations in the Greater Rochester NY area\" at 6920 Mt. Morris/Nunda Road (Route 408); tent and RV sites and cabin rental, a swimming pool, four playgrounds, catch-and-release fishing ponds, nine-hole disc golf and the Owls Nest Cafe; Columbus Day and closing weekend events in October 2026"},{"name":"Dream Lake Campground, Wyoming County","source":"https://dreamlakecampground.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"own website online reservations; phone (585) 786-5172","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"\"Located in the rolling hills of Wyoming County\", run by Keith and Patty Jarnot since 2015 \"with a 46 site expansion in 2021\"; canoe, kayak or fish on the lake and themed weekends; \"conveniently located close to Letchworth State Park\""},{"name":"Letchworth Valley Campground & Resort, Bliss","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/camping-in-new-york/near-letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"Campspot online booking","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Campspot: \"sprawls across 147 acres\" with \"a private lake and natural creek\", tent, RV and cabin options, and The Lodge at Wiscoy Lake for weddings and meetings; Hipcamp lists it \"10 minutes from Letchworth Park\" with \"Wiscoy Creek famous for trout fishing\""},{"name":"Yogi Bear''s Jellystone Park of Western New York, North Java","source":"https://www.campspot.com/c/camping-in-new-york/near-letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family"],"booking_route":"Campspot online booking","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Campspot: \"over 100 acres of serene pine forest in the heart of North Java\", full-hookup RV sites, tent sites and cabin rentals, swimming pool, mini-golf and playgrounds; Campspot Awards 2025 \"Top for Families\" winner"},{"name":"Glamping in Perry Near Letchworth (Hipcamp)","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/new-york-glamping-in-perry-near-letchworth-9mxhywzd","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp online booking","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"12 acres in Perry with Golden Hour Glamping, \"a bell canvas tent sleeping 4\" with queen bed and solar/battery electricity, and Honeysuckle Hideaway, \"an A-frame luxury cabin sleeping up to 6\" with mini-split heat and AC; outhouse with shower; a 2-3 minute walk from parking with a wagon for luggage"},{"name":"Perry and Silver Lake","source":"https://iloveperryny.com/visitors","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - a public village and beach","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["shop"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"the village reached from the park''s Perry exit: \"Follow St. Helena Street into Perry\"; \"main\" Main Street shops including Burlingham Books, South Main Street''s Hole in the Wall, Charcoal Corral and Silver Lake Twin Drive-in, a village park and public beach on Silver Lake; area stays listed by the village include Perry Bed & Breakfa