_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","activities"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"restaurant, pizzeria, ice cream parlor with \"34 Flavors of 100% All Natural Perry''s Ice Cream\", arcade, mini-golf and a twin drive-in; Italian Night all-you-can-eat pasta on Wednesdays and Seafood Friday; Halloween Family Fun Night Saturday, October 24, 2026"},{"name":"The Hole in the Wall Arcade & Lounge, Perry","source":"https://www.holeinthewallperry.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family","group"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone 585-237-3003","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"\"Wood-fired pizza, chicken wings, snacks and dessert. Local craft beer, cider, wine and cocktails\", with pool, darts, pinball and video games; Thursday-Saturday from 4pm, Sunday from 12pm, at 7056 Standpipe Rd"},{"name":"Arcade & Attica Railroad, Arcade","source":"https://www.aarailroad.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["rail","family","culture","senior"],"booking_route":"own website online tickets","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"\"New York State''s only regularly operating steam-engine passenger excursion rides\", with \"107-year-old Steam Engine #18\" and \"vintage WWII era coaches\"; listed on the National Register of Historic Places; \"Fall Foliage Steam Excursions October 3rd - 21st\", two trains a day on October weekends"},{"name":"Byrncliff Golf Resort, Varysburg","source":"https://byrncliff.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["golf","group","romance"],"booking_route":"own website tee times and stay-and-play; phone (585) 535-7300","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["activities","stay","eat"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"\"a scenic, fun and challenging public 18 hole par 72 golf course, 20K of groomed skiing trails (rentals available)\", a bar and restaurant and \"only 25 rooms inclusive of the Maple Lodge\"; Stay & Play packages; 2357 Humphrey Road"},{"name":"Houghton / Letchworth KOA Holiday","source":"https://koa.com/states-provinces/new-york/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"koa.com ''Reserve / Check Rates''; phone 1-585-567-4211","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"listed by KOA among its New York campgrounds as \"Houghton / Letchworth KOA Holiday\" (KOA''s Holiday segment) in Houghton, New York; phone 1-585-567-4211, info@houghtonkoa.com; reserve and check rates through koa.com"},{"name":"Hampton Inn Geneseo","source":"https://www.geneseo.edu/?p=84078","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"Listed by SUNY Geneseo among hotels for its inauguration at \"4242 Lakeville Road, Geneseo, NY 14454\", phone 585-447-9040. Hilton''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Fairfield Inn & Suites by Marriott Batavia","source":"https://hotelguides.com/place-maps/new-york/map-batavia-ny-hotels.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides among Batavia hotels at \"4333 Federal Drive, I-90, Exit 48, Batavia, NY 14020\". Marriott''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Hampton Inn Batavia","source":"https://hotelguides.com/place-maps/new-york/map-batavia-ny-hotels.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":42,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides among Batavia hotels at \"4360 Commerce Drive, I-90, Exit 48, Batavia, NY 14020\". Hilton''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Sturdy footwear for the gorge rim trails","source":"https://nystateparks.blog/2019/11/19/ready-at-the-rope/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink) or amazon.com (Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":43,"blurb":"NY State Parks names Letchworth among the parks where rope rescues are \"becoming more common\": \"People fall while taking selfies, slip while wearing improper footwear, or enter hazardous and closed areas of our parks.\" Its advice: \"Wear sturdy yet comfortable shoes or boots, and bring water and snacks for the trail.\""},{"name":"Hiking poles for steep gorge terrain","source":"https://nystateparks.blog/2019/11/19/ready-at-the-rope/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to LEKI USA (AvantLink) or rei.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"NY State Parks: \"Be mindful during hikes on steep terrain or that go near cliff tops. Hiking poles can help stabilize yourself against a potential fall, and transfer stress of hiking from your knees and legs to your arms and back.\""},{"name":"Headlamp for the short fall and winter days","source":"https://nystateparks.blog/tag/hiking-safety/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to Black Diamond (AvantLink) or rei.com","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"NY State Parks: \"Some patrons fail to dress for the weather, do not bring flashlights or maps, fail to bring enough water\" (https://nystateparks.blog/2019/11/19/ready-at-the-rope/); \"tossing a flashlight or headlamp into your backpack is a good form of insurance, should you unexpectedly find yourself on the trail as dusk approaches.\""},{"name":"Winter traction for icy trails","source":"https://nystateparks.blog/2019/11/19/ready-at-the-rope/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink) or amazon.com (Associates)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"NY State Parks: \"In the winter, when snow and ice can cover trails, carry and use traction gear on boots, such a webbed spikes or crampons.\" Letchworth stays open in winter for snow tubing, cross-country skiing and snowmobiling."},{"name":"River Dog Fly Shop, Houghton","source":"https://www.breakawayclassicadventures.com/SHOP/RiverDog.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","wildlife"],"booking_route":"walk-in shop in Houghton; contact via the shop page","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","shop"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"\"Western New York''s Premier Fly Fishing Outfitter\", with local water notes for the Genesee River and Wiscoy and East Koy creeks: \"We have some great nymphing rods by Orvis and Douglas\" and \"lots of sink tip lines and flurocarbon leaders and tippet material in stock\". Contact Indrek at the shop."}],"faq":[{"q":"How much does it cost to get into Letchworth State Park?","a":"NYS Parks lists the vehicle entrance fee as \"$10 per vehicle (car, truck, van, motorcycle, etc)\" and \"All Buses $35\", with \"Pool & Museum included!\" The $80 Empire Pass gives unlimited day-use entry at most State Parks facilities.","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When does Letchworth State Park stop charging?","a":"For 2026 the park lists the vehicle fee as collected \"5/8/26 - 10/18/26: 9 am - 5 pm, daily.\"","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Which entrance is best for Letchworth State Park?","a":"It depends on what you want to see. The park lists the Portageville Entrance (South) for \"Access to the Glen Iris Inn, Museum, Middle and Upper Falls Area, and the Genesee Arch Bridge\"; the Castile Entrance (South) for the Archery Field Overlook, the Lower Falls Area, A and B Cabins and the Humphrey Nature Center; the Mt Morris Entrance (North) for the G.W. Harvey Swimming Pool and Highbanks Recreation Area; and the Perry Entrance (West) for \"Direct access to Highbanks Camping Area\".","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Letchworth State Park?","a":"Yes, with limits. \"A maximum of two pets are allowed in camping loops 100, 200, 700 and 800, Cabin Area C and day use areas unless prohibited by sign or directive.\" Pets must be \"crated or on a leash not more than 6-feet in length\", proof of rabies inoculation is required at check-in, and pets are not permitted in playgrounds, buildings, boardwalks or pools (service animals excepted).","source":"https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/letchworth-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Letchworth State Park?","a":"Only in the pool. \"Swimming is only permitted at the Harvey Swimming Pool on the North end of the park\"; \"Entry to the pool is free. Regular vehicle admission fees to enter the park still apply. Swimming in the Genesee River is prohibited.\" NYS Parks lists the 2026 pool season as \"Projected opening 6/27 - Labor Day\", 11:00 am-6:45 pm.","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/letchworth-state-park-faqs","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is peak foliage at Letchworth State Park?","a":"The county tourism office names \"Peak Leaf Season – Columbus Day weekend and the following weekends\", when \"traffic is very slow and congested\" and park management \"may close portions of the park due to congestion/overcrowding.\"","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/weddings-at-letchworth","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Letchworth State Park open in the winter?","a":"Yes. \"The park is open 6am-11pm. However, there are various seasonal winter closures to be aware of.\" There is a tubing hill near Trailside Lodge (bring your own inflatable tube), snowmobiling on designated trails, and cross-country skiing and snowshoeing \"as conditions allow.\"","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/letchworth-state-park-faqs","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fly a drone in Letchworth State Park?","a":"Only with a permit. \"Drones can be used by permit only in certain areas of the park. Fees and insurance requirements apply.\" Call the park visitor center at (585) 493-3600.","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/letchworth-state-park-faqs","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you get married at Letchworth State Park?","a":"Yes. \"Getting married at the park is free; however, it is asked that bridal parties call the visitor''s center at (585) 493.3600 to ensure area availability for the event. Regular vehicle admission fees apply and additional permits may be required.\" The Glen Iris Inn also hosts weddings overlooking Middle Falls.","source":"https://www.exploreletchworth.com/explore-letchworth-state-park/letchworth-state-park-faqs","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How far is Letchworth State Park from Niagara Falls?","a":"Adventure Bound Four Winds, a campground in Portageville next to the park, states that from its site \"Rochester, New York ... is 45 minutes north. Buffalo is 60 minutes north. Niagara Falls is 75 minutes away.\" These are the campground''s own drive times, not a park or transport-authority figure.","source":"https://abcamping.com/abfourwinds/camping-near-letchworth-state-park-ny.php","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Letchworth State Park: Grand Canyon of the East, Waterfalls & Glen Iris Inn | TravelWell","meta_description":"Letchworth, the ''Grand Canyon of the East'': three Genesee River waterfalls, 66 miles of trails, cabins, the Glen Iris Inn and 2026 fall shuttle dates.","slug":"letchworth-state-park-new-york","primary_keyword":"Letchworth State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Letchworth State Park waterfalls"}}'::jsonb, 37)
